    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nApartment 54, Pakenham House is a stylish and well-maintained one-bedroom duplex apartment set within the ever-popular Spencer Dock development. Benefitting from a dedicated concierge service and a superb range of local amenities on its doorstep.\n\nLocated on the ground floor, No. 54 offers bright and spacious accommodation throughout. The welcoming entrance hallway provides access to a convenient guest WC. The open-plan living and dining area is filled with natural light through impressive floor-to-ceiling windows, while the contemporary kitchen is neatly positioned to the rear of the space. Upstairs, the generous double bedroom features built-in wardrobes and a modern en-suite bathroom.\n\nIdeally situated in the heart of the IFSC, the property enjoys immediate access to a wide selection of amenities and services. A short stroll across the Samuel Beckett Bridge brings you to Grand Canal Dock, home to the Bord Gáis Energy Theatre along with an excellent choice of cafés, restaurants, and bars. The area is exceptionally well connected with Dublin Bus routes, taxi services, and the Spencer Dock LUAS stop all nearby, while the M50 and Port Tunnel are also easily accessible. In addition, some of Dublin's best shopping destinations, including Henry Street and the Jervis Shopping Centre, are within walking distance, making this property an ideal city residence or investment opportunity."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.420m x 1.920m\nWelcoming entrance hall with a laminate wooden floor and access to guest wc.\n\nLiving/Dining Room - 4.395m x 4.876m\nBright and spacious open-plan living room with a laminate wooden floor, floor to ceiling windows with access to the outdoor terrace, spiral staircase to the mezzanine bedroom.\n\nKitchen - 1.774m x 2.586m\nModern kitchen off the living/dining room with a tiled floor, ample storage in the floor and wall-mounted cupboards, plumbed for washing machine, integrated fridge/freezer and dishwasher, oven and hob.\n\nBedroom - 4.402m x 3.761m\nSpacious double bedroom with laminate wooden flooring with built-in wardrobes and access to the ensuite bathroom.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.346m x 1.802m\nFully tiled bathroom with wc, whb, bath and shower.\n\nBathroom - 2.192m x 0.921m\nAccessed via the hallway, fully tiled with wc.\n\n"
      },
